# Rail-optimized fabric for 16 HGX nodes x 8 GPUs = 128 NICs (Wang et al.,
# arXiv 2307.12169, Fig. 1/3 "rail-optimized"), expressed as a 2-tier
# leaf-spine. Physical graph: 8 leaf (= rail) switches with 16 host ports and
# 16 uplinks each, 16 spines with one link to every leaf, 100 Gbps, 1:1.
#
# HTSIM wires host h to leaf h/16 (fat_tree_topology.h HOST_POD_SWITCH).
# The graph is the same as an ordinary 128-host leaf-spine; what makes it
# rail-optimized is the host labelling used in the traffic matrix:
#   rail labelling          host = 16*gpu_index + node   (leaf i = rail i)
#   conventional labelling  host = 8*node + gpu_index    (leaf = 2 nodes)
# See docs/TOPOLOGY_RAIL.md.
Nodes 128
Tiers 2
Podsize 128

Tier 0
Oversubscribed 1
Downlink_speed_Gbps 100
Radix_Down 16
Radix_Up 16
Downlink_Latency_ns 1000
Switch_Latency_ns 0

Tier 1
Downlink_speed_Gbps 100
Radix_Down 8
Downlink_Latency_ns 1000
Switch_Latency_ns 0
